WEBVTT

00:10.710 --> 00:14.695
So many fried buns…

00:14.773 --> 00:17.757
I hope you suffocate in a pile of fried buns!

00:17.821 --> 00:18.546
Ouch!

01:56.703 --> 02:01.867
Welcome! Thank you for coming, Blue Beyond…?

02:02.410 --> 02:04.414
It's been a year, hasn't it, Chief?

02:04.586 --> 02:07.921
Uh, where are the others?

02:08.218 --> 02:12.820
They recently left the group.
Alma and I are the only members now.

02:13.867 --> 02:17.640
Don't worry. We'll drive the thieves out
by the end of the day.

02:21.773 --> 02:24.179
Here. Have a cup of tea.

02:25.664 --> 02:26.875
It's been a while.

02:28.789 --> 02:32.007
I'm sorry. You know how kids her age are.

02:32.109 --> 02:36.140
She was looking forward to
seeing all of you, actually.

02:36.305 --> 02:38.585
Sorry about that.

02:38.781 --> 02:42.015
She must be disappointed that
our handsome leader isn't here.

02:42.195 --> 02:44.593
No, that's not it.

02:44.867 --> 02:45.461
- My daughter always talked about…

02:45.462 --> 02:47.062
- Noel…
- My daughter always talked about…

02:47.766 --> 02:49.429
Let's go over the agreement.

02:50.125 --> 02:53.281
Your letter says there are about twenty thieves.

02:53.555 --> 02:57.507
The neighboring village has already been attacked,
resulting in several fatalities.

02:57.758 --> 03:02.546
They've taken not only money and goods,
but young girls… Truly awful.

03:03.078 --> 03:06.968
You say they're drifters.
Have you located their base?

03:07.070 --> 03:09.679
Yes. It's in a rocky area
in the woods to the east.

03:10.298 --> 03:12.342
That's all the info I need.

03:13.063 --> 03:14.735
Let's talk compensation.

03:15.055 --> 03:18.351
As we agreed, I'll get 200,000 fil upfront

03:18.508 --> 03:22.109
and 300,000 after the job is done
for a total of 500,000.

03:22.641 --> 03:25.070
Here's the 200,000 upfront.

03:25.531 --> 03:26.937
You can make sure it's all there.

03:27.103 --> 03:31.664
That was easy. I thought he'd hem
and haw a bit more.

03:32.477 --> 03:35.945
It looks like it took some frugal living
to scrape this together.

03:36.289 --> 03:39.210
It's all there. Then after the job's done…

03:39.353 --> 03:41.414
I-I'll pay you then!

03:42.097 --> 03:45.328
We'll be off. Just take it easy and wait.

03:49.430 --> 03:53.171
That balding man kept staring at my boobs.

03:53.328 --> 03:55.150
Huh? He did?

03:55.312 --> 03:58.484
With his wife and daughter
right there. What a creep.

03:58.579 --> 04:00.000
Noel!

04:02.625 --> 04:05.679
Um… You're going to hunt down the bad guys, right?

04:06.039 --> 04:09.554
Yeah. I'll be done right away. Rest assured.

04:10.148 --> 04:13.531
U-Um… Y-You can do it!

04:13.797 --> 04:14.945
I'm rooting for you!

04:15.180 --> 04:15.882
Huh?

04:16.429 --> 04:18.093
Oh… Thanks.

04:20.156 --> 04:21.546
You can have this.

04:21.867 --> 04:27.585
A bamboo-copter? Right, I taught you
how to make these when I was last here.

04:27.835 --> 04:33.742
Yes! Mine fly higher than
the ones all the other kids make!

04:33.820 --> 04:34.906
Like fwoosh!

04:35.523 --> 04:37.070
But this is…

04:37.531 --> 04:40.351
the bamboo-copter you gave me then.

04:40.508 --> 04:42.265
I've kept it ever since.

04:43.352 --> 04:46.539
It's like a treasure to me!

04:46.945 --> 04:48.375
I'm glad to hear that.

04:49.680 --> 04:51.492
So, um…

04:52.380 --> 04:53.600
I'll be waiting for you!

04:53.744 --> 04:57.800
My mommy and I will make
a big feast for when you get back!

05:00.953 --> 05:02.960
What's that look for?

05:03.132 --> 05:06.171
You nasty pretty boy.

05:06.563 --> 05:11.211
You've got that innocent girl
wrapped around your finger. I'm amazed.

05:11.367 --> 05:13.726
Shut up, tits-for-brains.

05:13.984 --> 05:17.007
Tits-for-brains?! Are you talking about me?!

05:17.187 --> 05:18.953
Let's go find those thieves!

05:19.046 --> 05:23.187
Wait! I can't just let that slide!

05:30.930 --> 05:34.429
Why did that bald pervert say there are twenty?

05:35.125 --> 05:37.101
There are obviously twice as many.

05:37.492 --> 05:42.281
No mere drifter could gather a group this large.

05:42.906 --> 05:45.164
That must be their boss.

05:46.648 --> 05:48.304
He looks familiar.

05:48.867 --> 05:51.343
I know. That's Gordo the Razor Blade.

05:52.023 --> 05:52.929
Who?

05:53.087 --> 05:55.204
He has a bounty of 2 million fil on his head.

05:55.297 --> 05:57.960
So he's still alive. Stubborn fellow.

05:58.461 --> 06:01.562
Gordo is a B-Rank Scout who's a Bandit.

06:01.913 --> 06:02.742
Can you beat him?

06:03.000 --> 06:07.882
Easily, one-on-one. But not if
the others fight alongside him.

06:08.312 --> 06:10.718
Yeah. I'll deal with them.

06:10.914 --> 06:13.289
You're going to fight too?

06:13.547 --> 06:17.523
But if we get any closer,
the bandits will spot us.

06:17.883 --> 06:20.445
I have a Skill to conceal myself, but…

06:20.554 --> 06:22.804
Let me finish.

06:23.445 --> 06:24.804
I have a plan.

06:27.727 --> 06:28.727
Stealth.

06:30.094 --> 06:31.094
Are you ready?

06:32.055 --> 06:35.593
Getting into position now. Also, this is handy.

06:36.133 --> 06:36.438
[Thought Sharing]

06:36.438 --> 06:38.320
[Thought Sharing]
Thought Sharing. Link.

06:38.320 --> 06:39.008
[Thought Sharing]

06:39.009 --> 06:41.992
[Thought Sharing]
We can communicate long distance using this.

06:41.992 --> 06:42.789
[Thought Sharing]

06:42.790 --> 06:43.789
[Thought Sharing]
I'm there.

06:45.180 --> 06:46.664
Ten meters away.

06:46.945 --> 06:49.398
I can go as soon as you give the order.

06:49.906 --> 06:50.750
Roger that.

06:51.969 --> 06:53.750
I'm using Stun Howl!

06:54.816 --> 06:55.929
[Wolf's Howl]
Stop!

06:57.609 --> 06:59.328
Hey! What happened?!

06:59.904 --> 07:02.112
Order! Kill Gordo!

07:02.492 --> 07:04.160
Accel Quintuple.

07:05.440 --> 07:06.736
Quick Attack!

07:15.552 --> 07:17.872
Confirmed dead. Next order.

07:18.312 --> 07:20.765
Keep the enemies distracted until I'm there!

07:21.156 --> 07:22.048
Roger that.

07:29.680 --> 07:32.736
That moron is having fun killing.

07:33.264 --> 07:35.056
She's going to be trouble.

07:37.040 --> 07:38.000
Eleven!

07:38.624 --> 07:39.265
Alma!

07:39.370 --> 07:40.720
I'm almost there!

07:40.976 --> 07:42.352
Using a flash bomb!

07:42.736 --> 07:44.400
G-Got it!

07:46.752 --> 07:48.128
Flame Bullet!

08:03.812 --> 08:06.832
Would you look at that!
Good to see you back safely!

08:08.820 --> 08:11.600
So, the gang of thieves…

08:12.910 --> 08:16.048
All dead. Here's the boss's head.

08:16.593 --> 08:17.504
Care to look?

08:17.960 --> 08:19.792
N-No…

08:20.132 --> 08:22.512
I'll be taking the rest of the money.

08:22.704 --> 08:27.000
Y-Yes, of course! But please
stay for dinner first!

08:27.367 --> 08:33.312
My wife and daughter have
prepared a feast for you!

08:36.416 --> 08:38.496
Yes, that's right!

08:38.912 --> 08:42.703
She just got her appraisal,
and her Job is Swordsman!

08:42.800 --> 08:43.952
N-Noel!

08:44.112 --> 08:47.504
I want to be a great Seeker like you!

08:47.744 --> 08:49.500
Do you think I can do it?

08:49.904 --> 08:53.152
Any grown adult can be a Seeker.

08:53.320 --> 08:55.398
You only have to register officially.

08:55.859 --> 08:59.539
Then most people enroll at
the training school in the capital.

09:00.195 --> 09:02.035
Tuition is covered by the government.

09:02.883 --> 09:04.883
You'll spend two years if you're a front-liner,

09:05.027 --> 09:06.323
or one if you're a backliner.

09:06.883 --> 09:08.835
So I'd spend two years.

09:09.011 --> 09:14.227
But the cost of living is high in the capital.
That cost will fall on you.

09:15.011 --> 09:17.363
You'll have to save up before that.

09:17.891 --> 09:19.987
Really…?

09:20.499 --> 09:22.202
Well, this isn't what most people do,

09:22.288 --> 09:25.811
but you could also work
as an apprentice to build up experience.

09:25.987 --> 09:27.124
Really?!

09:27.199 --> 09:31.843
Yeah. Apprentices basically do
odd jobs for Seekers.

09:32.339 --> 09:34.963
You can get paid if you join
the Apprentice Association.

09:35.763 --> 09:38.739
And you'd get to see
professional combat in person.

09:44.355 --> 09:44.947
Um…

09:45.587 --> 09:47.891
If I become a powerful Seeker,

09:48.163 --> 09:50.147
could I join Blue Beyond?

09:51.123 --> 09:54.243
If you were really a powerful Seeker,

09:54.755 --> 09:59.139
and I could be sure I'd live up
to your expectations,

10:00.083 --> 10:01.747
then I'd be glad to fight alongside you.

10:02.083 --> 10:05.987
Really?! Then I promise I will!

10:06.179 --> 10:09.011
Good for you, Chelsea!

10:09.347 --> 10:11.331
Please, enjoy a glass.

10:11.619 --> 10:13.587
I brought this out just for you.

10:15.795 --> 10:18.403
A bottle of this goes for 100,000 fil.

10:18.899 --> 10:23.587
I've been saving it for a special occasion.

10:24.547 --> 10:28.307
So, to celebrate this new chapter
in Chelsea's life…

10:32.611 --> 10:34.275
This certainly is quality wine.

10:34.563 --> 10:36.819
I can tell by the color and fragrance.

10:36.899 --> 10:40.049
It is, isn't it? You don't get the chance
to drink wine like this often…

10:40.049 --> 10:44.403
I wouldn't feel right drinking
such a fine wine before you, sir.

10:44.739 --> 10:48.467
Please, as our host, have the first drink.

10:48.721 --> 10:51.475
Huh? M-Me…?

10:51.939 --> 10:53.347
Is there a problem with that?

10:53.571 --> 10:57.128
N-No! It's just… I don't drink.

10:57.259 --> 11:02.259
That's funny. Why would you buy a 100,000 fil
bottle of wine if you don't drink?

11:02.323 --> 11:04.451
W-Well…

11:04.531 --> 11:06.691
Go right ahead.

11:07.235 --> 11:08.819
Have a drink…

11:09.875 --> 11:12.112
of this poisoned wine.

11:12.867 --> 11:15.859
[IV - Don't Expect Forgiveness If You Say Sorry]

11:19.075 --> 11:21.395
P-P-Poisoned?!

11:21.395 --> 11:23.389
Why would I do such a thing?!

11:24.291 --> 11:27.939
Because you won't have to pay us if we die first.

11:28.627 --> 11:30.883
Then you could take our cash and equipment.

11:31.043 --> 11:33.259
You'd profit twice over.

11:33.339 --> 11:35.859
Absolutely not! How could you say such a thing?!

11:35.859 --> 11:38.354
- What proof do you…
- Three things.

11:39.347 --> 11:39.987
One.

11:40.659 --> 11:44.291
A man stingy enough to lie about
how many thieves there are

11:44.435 --> 11:47.603
wouldn't serve 100,000 fil wine.

11:49.363 --> 11:52.315
Two. This is cheap wine.

11:52.666 --> 11:56.550
And I can tell from the scent that it's not fresh.

11:57.075 --> 12:00.659
So you've already opened this some time ago.

12:00.947 --> 12:03.939
That means you couldn't have been
saving it for a special occasion.

12:04.355 --> 12:06.449
W-Well…

12:06.534 --> 12:12.003
Three. I've sensed hostility from you
ever since you brought out the wine.

12:13.251 --> 12:14.947
Noel is right.

12:15.171 --> 12:19.699
You were dumb if you thought you could
pull off a cheap trick like that on us.

12:19.891 --> 12:23.347
And Scouts are poison-resistant,
so it wouldn't even have worked.

12:23.475 --> 12:26.611
Shut up! What proof do you have?!

12:27.555 --> 12:30.947
Then drink the wine.

12:34.051 --> 12:36.003
Shut up, shut up, shut up!

12:36.198 --> 12:38.851
Who cares what you have to say?!

12:39.091 --> 12:42.509
Get out! Get out of my village!

12:42.509 --> 12:43.171
Confess.

12:45.507 --> 12:47.347
You poisoned the wine, didn't you?

12:47.507 --> 12:48.515
Spill it.

12:49.363 --> 12:52.051
Yes. I poisoned it.

12:52.243 --> 12:59.395
I meant to trick you dumb Seekers into
killing the thieves and then steal your valuables.

13:00.627 --> 13:02.099
D-Daddy…

13:02.995 --> 13:05.395
Were you really going to…?

13:15.229 --> 13:17.082
O-Owwow!

13:17.169 --> 13:19.763
My eye! My eye!

13:20.611 --> 13:23.043
Don't think I'll stop with one eye.

13:23.283 --> 13:24.947
The other one's next.

13:25.411 --> 13:28.099
Then I'll chop off your nose and ears.

13:28.099 --> 13:31.395
I'll break all your teeth and rip out your tongue.

13:32.179 --> 13:34.399
P-Please forgive me!

13:34.464 --> 13:35.923
Forgive you?

13:35.987 --> 13:40.307
You expect to be forgiven for
attempted murder if you just say sorry?

13:40.403 --> 13:44.739
I-I can get the money to you
right away! 300,000 fil…

13:44.815 --> 13:47.599
300,000? Don't make me laugh.

13:47.599 --> 13:49.427
You think that'll make up for this?

13:49.667 --> 13:52.643
If you want help, give me all your money.

13:53.251 --> 13:56.315
I-I can't! I'm in debt…

13:57.059 --> 13:58.915
No more negotiating.

14:02.723 --> 14:06.931
This is the last light you'll ever see.

14:07.219 --> 14:09.379
Take it in before…

14:09.379 --> 14:11.604
It's the Gambino family!

14:12.563 --> 14:16.029
I'm in debt to the Gambino family!

14:16.029 --> 14:17.569
The mob!

14:17.569 --> 14:21.491
They'll kill me if I miss a payment!

14:21.875 --> 14:23.699
Why should I care?

14:23.699 --> 14:25.699
Don't disrespect Seekers.

14:29.155 --> 14:30.739
Wait! Please!

14:30.739 --> 14:34.307
This is all our money! 820,000 fil in all!

14:34.547 --> 14:36.299
We don't have one copper more!

14:36.883 --> 14:40.611
You can have it, so let my daddy go!

14:40.819 --> 14:46.319
Stupid girl! Do you know what the Gambinos will
do to me if I give that money…

14:46.393 --> 14:48.870
But if I don't, then he's going to…!

14:48.956 --> 14:51.491
B-But…

14:55.699 --> 14:58.883
I'm telling the truth! Please, take it!

15:05.043 --> 15:06.227
Alma. Let's go.

15:06.531 --> 15:07.251
Sure thing.

15:08.589 --> 15:14.753
It's over! It's all over…!

15:15.795 --> 15:17.907
I hate you…

15:18.227 --> 15:19.667
I hate you!

15:20.275 --> 15:22.579
I hate Seekers!

15:31.331 --> 15:33.891
Seekers are pettier than I expected.

15:34.227 --> 15:36.739
Are you sick of it already?

15:36.995 --> 15:38.435
I'm not sick of it.

15:38.915 --> 15:40.003
That's good, then.

15:41.299 --> 15:43.283
What about you? Are you okay?

15:43.603 --> 15:44.435
I'm fine.

15:44.691 --> 15:52.995
Okay. I just thought it must hurt to
disappoint a girl who looked up to you.

15:53.427 --> 15:57.267
If I was afraid of disappointing people,
I'd go live on a desert island.

15:57.507 --> 16:01.059
You can tell your big sister
if you ever have difficult feelings.

16:01.059 --> 16:02.563
I'll give you a hug.

16:02.771 --> 16:05.603
Go hug a cactus, tits-for-brains.

16:06.131 --> 16:09.167
Did you just call me tits-for-brains
again?! Stop that!

16:09.245 --> 16:12.211
Then stop treating me like a kid.

16:13.603 --> 16:14.787
That won't be easy.

16:15.107 --> 16:17.379
It's your fault for being so cute.

16:17.763 --> 16:19.123
What kind of logic is that?

16:23.354 --> 16:26.787
Ooh, an airship!

16:26.803 --> 16:27.731
It's huge!

16:28.083 --> 16:32.691
That's Goat Dinner's symbol.
They're a three-star regalia clan.

16:33.059 --> 16:34.147
Regalia?

16:34.483 --> 16:35.779
What's that?

16:36.115 --> 16:40.227
A rank granted by the emperor
to clans recognized for their ability.

16:40.402 --> 16:41.842
[Seven Stars]

16:41.843 --> 16:43.939
[Seven Stars]
Seven clans can have regalia at a time.

16:43.939 --> 16:44.739
[Seven Stars]

16:44.739 --> 16:46.859
[Seven Stars]
And they aren't all equal.

16:46.859 --> 16:50.019
[Seven Stars]
They're ranked by their strength
and accomplishments.

16:50.883 --> 16:53.219
From the bottom, there are four three-star clans,

16:53.539 --> 16:55.075
two two-star clans,

16:55.587 --> 16:57.299
and one one-star clan.

16:57.523 --> 17:01.107
Airships are one special privilege
clans with regalia get.

17:01.587 --> 17:03.139
That's awesome!

17:03.139 --> 17:06.323
So that airship is full of strong Seekers?

17:06.851 --> 17:08.371
They're more than just strong.

17:08.819 --> 17:11.875
They're knowledgeable, experienced,
wealthy, and courageous.

17:12.035 --> 17:14.755
Any one picked at random
would be a world-class Seeker.

17:16.387 --> 17:17.315
I've decided.

17:20.547 --> 17:21.859
In a year's time…

17:23.267 --> 17:25.203
We're going to have regalia.

17:28.963 --> 17:31.427
So? Do I pass?

17:31.747 --> 17:32.787
You pass.

17:33.427 --> 17:34.835
The combat test, at least.

17:35.443 --> 17:37.027
Is there more?

17:37.739 --> 17:41.427
Just answer one simple question.

17:42.563 --> 17:47.011
Did you kill our former leader Alcor Judikhali?

17:48.115 --> 17:49.123
I did.

17:49.619 --> 17:52.515
Not even the god of killing
could fight when his mind is gone.

17:52.675 --> 17:54.259
He was an easy kill.

17:54.835 --> 17:56.115
Why did you kill him?

17:56.707 --> 17:58.483
Do you need to ask?

17:59.667 --> 18:01.475
No. That was a silly question.

18:03.395 --> 18:06.307
Alcor was a deeply terrifying man.

18:06.835 --> 18:12.019
He sought power for power's sake,
and so he became a harbinger of death.

18:12.379 --> 18:16.307
Alcor was a reaper in human guise.

18:16.819 --> 18:19.309
But he lost to Overdeath.

18:19.401 --> 18:20.867
Yes. He lost.

18:21.427 --> 18:24.189
He had absolute power,

18:24.189 --> 18:26.451
and yet there was one man even he could not outdo.

18:27.571 --> 18:32.099
That realization was the beginning
of Alcor's mental breakdown.

18:33.811 --> 18:36.963
Alma, you aren't Alcor's granddaughter.

18:37.331 --> 18:38.355
You're his daughter.

18:38.835 --> 18:39.859
I am.

18:41.091 --> 18:47.747
I'm one of the children he fathered with
a woman he abducted from some village.

18:48.451 --> 18:53.235
But what he wanted was someone just like himself.

18:53.651 --> 18:56.963
No. He just wanted a new him.

18:57.747 --> 19:02.387
He never escaped the fear of defeat.

19:02.979 --> 19:06.355
So he decided to make a new him
who would never lose.

19:06.867 --> 19:09.656
He genuinely believed that
by doing that, he could erase

19:09.657 --> 19:12.963
the dark mark on his past
that was his loss to Overdeath.

19:14.147 --> 19:18.707
My siblings all died for his warped delusion.

19:19.427 --> 19:23.779
I, his biggest success, was the only one left.

19:27.619 --> 19:30.083
Alma. I'll be honest with you.

19:30.435 --> 19:32.931
I don't have a place for you in this society.

19:33.267 --> 19:35.891
Why not?! You saw how strong I am!

19:36.147 --> 19:38.547
It's true that your power is remarkable.

19:39.075 --> 19:42.800
But whether you're a good fit
for the Society is another question.

19:42.899 --> 19:46.387
I don't understand! Explain it to me!

19:47.427 --> 19:49.731
This stays between you and me.

19:50.131 --> 19:54.627
We aren't going to stop killing
once we're an official government organization.

19:55.571 --> 19:58.227
But whereas killing was our end before,

19:58.739 --> 20:01.283
killing will serve as a means from now on.

20:01.859 --> 20:04.675
Those may sound similar,
but there's a big difference.

20:05.267 --> 20:08.275
The latter kind of killing,
at least, has a future.

20:09.988 --> 20:11.096
A future…?

20:17.171 --> 20:21.363
This is what I get for
twenty-one years of forced training?

20:22.099 --> 20:25.027
A titan sleeps within your heart.

20:25.091 --> 20:27.315
You'd be a danger to the Society.

20:28.051 --> 20:31.843
I never had anything fun.

20:32.595 --> 20:35.731
I had no friends. No lovers.

20:36.755 --> 20:39.411
All I ever did…

20:39.811 --> 20:41.599
was try to survive.

20:41.599 --> 20:43.171
And now… I'm not needed?

20:43.251 --> 20:44.609
I'm not good enough?

20:44.609 --> 20:50.691
Then what did I go through all that for?
What were those twenty-one years for?

20:53.299 --> 20:54.371
Give it back…

20:55.315 --> 20:57.099
Give it back!

20:57.099 --> 20:59.587
Give me back my life!

21:02.131 --> 21:04.595
Wait! What am I supposed to do?!

21:05.523 --> 21:07.059
Live however you like.

21:11.907 --> 21:14.355
Right, I have something interesting to tell you.

21:14.963 --> 21:18.691
Overdeath's grandson is working
as a Seeker in the capital.

21:21.203 --> 21:24.019
Overdeath's grandson? Is he strong?

21:24.595 --> 21:26.243
Yes, rather strong.

21:26.675 --> 21:29.283
But his Job is Talker.

21:30.915 --> 21:31.891
A Talker…!

21:32.163 --> 21:34.739
As everyone knows, it's the weakest Job.

21:36.307 --> 21:38.659
You could go talk to him if you're interested.

21:39.331 --> 21:40.323
His name is…

21:42.163 --> 21:43.699
Noel Stollen.

21:53.891 --> 21:54.547
Alma?

21:57.235 --> 21:58.243
I'll always…

21:59.267 --> 22:02.019
I'll always fight alongside you!

23:34.882 --> 23:40.031
[V - Swordsman of the Far East]
